CROSS-CUTTING NOTES — patterns noticed while going through all 36 cities (splatter_1 through 7), plus
standout candidates worth promoting to the polished Weapon_Item_Catalog.md eventually. Not organized, just
flagging what jumped out.

RECURRING MOTIFS (the same underlying tool-shape shows up city after city — worth deciding whether these
should be ONE catalog entry each with many cities' worth of flavor text, rather than 8+ near-duplicate items):
- Cargo/dock hooks — Marambio, Sanay, Janbogo, Zukelli, Casey, Byrd, Cape Adare, Esperanza, Juan Carlos all
  have some version of this. One generic "Cargo Hook" item, flavored per-district, probably beats 9 separate
  near-identical entries.
- Chains/cables/tow-lines — Marambio, Belgrano, Lazar, Sanay, Troll, Sayowa. Same logic as above.
- Ice-core/deep-drilling tools — already a Bladed Melee catalog item, but Vostok's version is a genuine
  outlier (deepest, most extreme, 25-million-year-sealed-lake stakes) and probably deserves its own named
  variant rather than folding into the generic entry.
- Hospitality/serving implements (kettle, tray, carving tools) — Palmer City, Janbogo, Zukelli, Juan Carlos,
  Mawson all have a version. Worth one strong "Serving Implement" item with per-city flavor rather than five
  near-duplicates.
- Wind-engineering struts/anchors — Denison, Dumont d'Urville, Princess Elisabeth, Mirny (Windbreak Turbine
  Fragment, already catalogued). Same consolidation logic.

STANDOUT, GENUINELY UNIQUE CANDIDATES (worth individual promotion, not generic):
- Byrd's salvaged aircraft propeller-blade fragment — real narrative weight (the connection to the rest of
  Tepenia that no longer works), nothing else in the roster has this specific emotional charge
- Scott's volcanic-ash collection tongs — the single most geographically/scientifically specific item in the
  whole set (Mount Erebus fallout, one city's one real industry)
- Halley's relocation-rig cable/winch — the literal mechanism of a city that physically moves; unmatched
  anywhere else
- Vostok's deep ice-core drill — see above, the extremity is the point
- Zukelli's post-destruction salvage framing — the only city in the roster whose gear should read as
  scavenged-from-ruins rather than actively-in-use; worth deciding whether this framing extends to any other
  war-damaged city or stays unique to Zukelli
- Dome Fuji's religious/pilgrimage implement — the only genuinely devotional item in the whole set; needs
  careful, specific writing rather than generic "monastery prop" treatment

OPEN QUESTION FOR WHOEVER ORGANIZES THIS NEXT: should the final gear_collection_DRAFT_-_weapons.md be
organized by CITY (36 entries, matching this brainstorm's own structure) or by WEAPON CATEGORY (folding each
city's contribution into Weapon_Item_Catalog.md's existing 13-category structure, the way the Zhongshan/
Mirny/Sinheung items already were)? The category structure is probably the better long-term home given how
much overlap exists between cities (see Recurring Motifs above), but the city-by-city structure is what makes
each item's specific origin story legible. Possibly both: category-organized in the main catalog, with a
per-city index pointing back at which items came from where.
